  "track": "track-01",
  "title": "delegates events lambdas closures and expression trees",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "A delegate is a type-safe object that represents one or more callable methods. It lets an API accept behavior as a value; invocation follows the delegate signature and multicast delegates invoke an ordered invocation list.",
    "An event exposes controlled subscription to a notification. Subscribers can add or remove handlers, while only the declaring type can raise a field-like event; event lifetime and unsubscription affect object retention.",
    "A lambda is an anonymous function expression whose target context supplies or helps infer its signature. Depending on the target, a lambda can become a delegate or an expression tree; these have different runtime meanings and capabilities.",
    "A closure is a function together with captured outer variables. Captured variables extend lifetimes and can change what later invocations observe. `static` lambdas prohibit captures and make that boundary explicit.",
    "An expression tree is a data representation of supported code, not executable code by itself. Providers can inspect and translate the tree; compiling an expression tree creates a delegate but may have runtime, trimming, or Native AOT constraints."
  ],
