  "accuracyFacts": [
    "Invoking a null delegate throws NullReferenceException; null-conditional invocation with ?.Invoke() skips the call when the delegate is null.",
    "For a multicast delegate with a non-void return, invocation returns the final invoked method's return value; intermediate return values are discarded. An exception stops normal progression through the invocation list.",
    "Expression trees represent supported expression structure for inspection or translation and differ from delegates that execute compiled code."
